      "text": "To determine the measure of \\(\\angle ACB\\) in degrees, we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the shape and angles in the diagram:**\n   - We have a quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\) that is outlined with points \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\).\n   - The problem gives us the following information:\n     - \\(\\angle ADC = 93^\\circ\\)\n     - \\(\\angle BCD = 130^\\circ\\)\n     - \\(D\\) is located at \\((-60, 0)\\), \\(B\\) at \\((0, 0)\\), and \\(C\\) at \\((166, 0)\\).\n     - We need to find \\(\\angle ACB\\).\n\n2. **Identify the relationship using angle sum property:**\n   - Since the sum of all angles in a quadrilateral is \\(360^\\circ\\),\n     \\[\n     \\angle DAC + \\angle BAC + \\angle CAD + \\angle ADC = 360^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n3. **Apply known angle relationships:**\n   - We know:\n     \\[\n     \\angle CAD + \\angle ADC = 53^\\circ \\quad (\\text{since} \\angle CAD + \\angle BCD = 130^\\circ \\text{and} \\angle BCD = 93^\\circ)\n     \\]\n   - Therefore,\n     \\[\n     \\angle DAC = 93^\\circ ( \\angle ADC is given as 93^\\circ)\n     \\]\n   \n4. **Step-by-step calculation:**\n   - Using the summation of angles property:\n     \\[\n     \\angle DAC + \\angle BAC + \\angle CAD + \\angle ADC = 360^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - Substitute \\( \\angle DAC \\) and other known values (since \\(\\angle BAC\\) and \\(\\angle CAD\\) are given):\n     \\[\n     93^\\circ + \\angle BAC + \\angle CAD + 93^\\circ = 360^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - Solving for \\(\\angle BAC + \\angle CAD\\):\n     \\[\n     186^\\circ + \\angle BAC + \\angle CAD = 360^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying, we get:\n     \\[\n     \\angle BAC + \\angle CAD = 174^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n5. **Determine the measure of \\(\\angle ACB$:**\n   - The remaining angle \\(\\angle BAC\\) is:\n     \\[\n     \\angle BAC = 93^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - The remaining angle \\(\\angle CAD\\) is:\n     \\[\n     \\angle CAD = \\angle BCD - \\angle BAC = 130^\\circ - 93^\\circ\n     \\]\n   - Finally, calculate \\(\\angle ADB\\):\n\n\\[\n\\angle ADB = 180^\\circ - \\angle ADC = 180^\\circ - 93^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle ACB\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{52^\\circ}\n\\]",
